hello everyone i'm dr umar malik and  welcome to my simplified i hope all of  you are doing well  before i start i would like to tell you  that our channel has recently crossed  900 000 subscribers and we are growing  day by day all thanks to you  i really appreciate the love and support  from you guys and we look forward to  cross more such milestones in the  upcoming future  so friends in today's video we will be  talking about the sunflower plant  scientifically known as helianthus anus  to be precise we will be talking about  the amazing health benefits of the  sunflower seeds  i'm pretty sure all of you have seen the  bright yellow flower of the sunflower  plant it's impossible to miss  the seeds are harvested from the head of  the sunflower plant  the flower head measures up to 12 inches  in diameter and one flowering head might  contain up to 2000 seeds  sunflower seeds are white but have a  tough outer shell  the shell is black and white with a  striped appearance  in many parts of the world including my  own which is india humans have been  consuming sunflower seeds since the time  immemorial in many forms  raw seeds are eaten as a portable and  easy snack  roasted seeds are sprinkled on top of  cereals cooked vegetables or salads  sunflower seeds can also be added to  breads or muffins  and oil and butter are obviously the  most common use of sunflower seeds  worldwide  well in this video we will talk about  some of the scientifically backed health  benefits of consuming sunflower seeds  so sit back relax and let me simplify it  for you  number one  sunflower seeds are densely packed with  nutrients  sunflower seeds are a wholesome food  this is because they are packed with a  good amount of healthy nutrients in  sufficient quantities  take for example just about 100 grams of  sunflower seeds contain 585 calories of  energy  mind you these are pure complex  carbohydrates which are considered as  good calories  they also contain about 8.5 grams of  fiber so just a wrist full of sunflower  seeds can meet the fiber demand of your  body  they contain about 51.5 grams of  essential fats and these are mostly  polyunsaturated and monounsaturated fats  which are known as good fats  these help in lowering your blood  cholesterol level and improve your  cardiovascular health  100 grams of sunflower seeds contain  about 20 grams of proteins  and they also contain micronutrients  such as thymine riboflavin niacin  pantothenic acid folate choline vitamin  b6 vitamin c and vitamin e  sunflower seeds also contain minerals  like calcium iron magnesium manganese  phosphorus potassium sodium and zinc  this information should be enough to  motivate you to start adding sunflower  seeds to your diet  before we proceed further in the video i  would like to take a minute to introduce  you all to yellow class  yellow class is india's biggest live and  interactive hobby learning platform  where kids can learn different hobbies  like art and craft dancing singing  cooking yoga and much more absolutely  free of cost  apart from these classes on maths  english general knowledge and logical  reasoning are also available on yellow  class  every month more than 10 lakh kids  attend various classes on yellow class  and learn various skills absolutely free  all the classes provided by yellow class  are completely free and they are  designed by professionals which are  experts in their field  special classes by celebrity mentors  like shaan ripudaman vidya malvade are  also available on yellow class  along with learning different hobbies on  yellow class kids can also win many  prizes like playstation apple ipad  bicycles amazon vouchers and much more  in february yellow class is running an  online contest where the winner can get  an apple iphone 13. in order to take  part in the contest all you have to do  is download the yellow class app using  the link given in the description box  down below and start attending the  classes  kids who will complete the above steps  will be automatically eligible for this  competition  number two sunflower seeds are good for  your heart  as i mentioned earlier sunflower seeds  are rich in fats now the word fats makes  people think about unhealthy stuff  but sunflower seeds are rich in healthy  fats including polyunsaturated fats and  monounsaturated fats  especially a compound known as linoleic  acid  linoleic acid is an essential fatty acid  it is very important because it is a  compound that relaxes blood vessels in  your body and also helps in lowering  your blood cholesterol level  this was clinically proven by a study at  harvard university  in 2014 a paper was published titled  consumption of plant seeds and  cardiovascular health epidemiologic and  clinical trial evidence  this summarized that there is  substantial evidence that increased seed  consumption including sunflower seeds is  associated with lower risk of  cardiovascular disease and type 2  diabetes  they meant that there is significant  reduction in the risk factors of heart  disease such as serum cholesterol levels  or high blood pressure which is  attributable to various components of  the sunflower seed  such as  niacin or vitamin v3 which is present in  sunflower seeds  it is an essential component of the  cholesterol pathways and it acts to  reduce the total cholesterol levels  vitamin b5 or pentothinic acid in  sunflower seeds increases hdl  which is healthy cholesterol  and it is required by the body  fiber present in the sunflower seeds  decreases the total fat absorption of  your body  magnesium which is an essential mineral  helps your blood vessels to relax and  eventually decreases the blood pressure  levels  cyanurine is an alkaloid found in the  sunflower seeds and it can lower  triglycerides and cholesterol levels  an effect that may potentially benefit  people with hyperglycemia or  hyperlipidemia  now this combined glucose and  cholesterol lowering effect of sunflower  seeds is especially important in people  with diabetes  some research like a 2012 study on  elderly females with type 2 diabetes  mellitus suggests that people who ate  sunflower seeds daily found their  fasting blood sugar reduced by up to 10  percent  but more research is required for wider  age group and better defined criteria  before sunflower seeds can be advocated  as a blood sugar lowering agent number  three sunflower seeds can boost your  immunity  sunflower seeds are packed with  essential vitamins and minerals  the most important of these for our  immunity are vitamin e  zinc and selenium  vitamin e is crucial to immune function  and helps to protect us against various  illnesses  it is a powerful antioxidant that helps  to prevent cell damage by free radicals  zinc is a key component of the immune  system and can help with the development  and maintenance of the immune cells  it also has antioxidant properties  a selenium also has natural  anti-inflammatory properties and it also  boosts the immune system to produce a  better immune response when required  this mineral is also postulated to be a  critical part of brain health  and is linked to prevention of various  neurodegenerative diseases such as  alzheimer's disease  now talking about brain health sunflower  seeds can also boost your brain function  sunflower seeds are a good source of  vitamin b6 also known as pyridoxine  this essential nutrient is important for  the synthesis of many neurotransmitters  in the brain  usually the imbalance of  neurotransmitters can lead to various  mental effects  so consumption of sunflower seeds can  restore the optimum balance  this helps to improve mood concentration  and memory  number four  sunflower seeds can reduce inflammation  in our previous videos we regularly talk  about the term inflammation  to clear a misconception inflammation  itself isn't bad it is a natural process  of our body that initiates in response  to injury or stress that occurs either  externally or internally  while in acute situations inflammation  is important for the body to control the  extent of damage and start the process  of healing and recovery  it is the chronic inflammation that is  proven to be harmful for us and chronic  inflammation is a risk factor for many  chronic diseases  one way researchers and doctors quantify  inflammation is by calculating the  levels of protein in a body known as c  reactive protein in short crp  increased crp levels in your body are a  signal for higher risk of inflammation  which is directly linked to the heart  disease and diabetes  a 2006 research titled nut and seed  consumption and inflammatory markers  attempted to find a relation between  consumption of seeds and nuts including  sunflower seeds and markers of  inflammation such as levels of crp  interleukin 6 and fibrinogen  they found that frequent nut and seed  consumption including sunflower seeds  was associated with lower levels of  inflammatory markers including crp  this also explained the association of  nut consumption with lower risk of  cardiovascular disease and diabetes  number five sunflower seeds are great  for pregnant females  sunflower seeds contain zinc folate and  vitamin e  these are all important nutrients for a  fetus to grow  so if you're trying to have a baby or  you are pregnant  or you're just someone following a  healthy diet sunflower seeds have  something for everyone  folate is a micronutrient with a very  important role in a developing baby  adequate folate levels are required for  the placenta to grow and remain healthy  also also folate is important for the  baby's brain and nervous system to grow  to its full potential folate deficiency  has been linked to terrible outcomes  such as spina bifida  zinc present in the sunflower seeds is  also important for the baby's pancreas  to produce insulin and other vital  enzymes  vitamin e present in these seeds is  essential for the fetus  it helps the muscles grow and also  supports the red blood cells which do  all the hard work of transporting vital  oxygen to each and every part of the  developing fetus  but wait  there's another benefit of sunflower  seeds  the healthy fatty acid the zinc and the  vitamin e gives you healthier skin  our skin is the first line of defense  against lethal diseases  it suffers from various external  destructive forces and regenerates  itself to keep the barrier strong  the essential fatty acids such as oleic  and linoleic acid found in the sunflower  seeds help prevent skin diseases  these compounds also help with the wound  healing and preventing scarring  so if you want a glowing complexion give  them a try  antibacterial and antifungal properties  of sunflower seeds also prevent  infections  thus keeping our skin clear  additionally zinc and vitamin e protect  the skin against uv damage and  accelerate skin regeneration  before i go there are some facts you  should be careful of  here are some potential side effects of  sunflower seeds  eating too many sulfur seeds can make  you vomit cause stomach ache and lead to  constipation  do not consume more than recommended  if you are allergic to some seeds  eating sunflower seeds can cause  vomiting rashes on the skin breathing  problems like wheezing or struggling to  breathe  sunflower seeds are high in calories  eating too many can lead to weight gain  sunflower seeds contain traces of  cadmium which are not good for our  kidneys so  moderate its consumption  also contaminated sprouts seeds can lead  to bacterial infections of the gut  as always it is important to wash your  hands before eating them  download the yellow class app now and  start your learning journey today well  friends with this we come to the end of  this video  i hope i have given you some new and  exciting facts and knowledge  if you liked today's video don't forget  to share it with your friends and family  if you are new to our channel consider  subscribing if you liked our content  we at med simplified always appreciate  your support and feedback  consider becoming a member of our  youtube channel or our patreon community  to support our channel  you can find us on instagram  search for med simplified on instagram  we post daily facts medical tidbits and  posts that will brighten your day  the links are in the description box  down below  as always take care and i'll see you in  the next one
 

